      "The shocking incursion did not have a significant impact on Israeli territory in 50 years. Reading Passage II The Disappearance of the Ancient City 1. For centuries, explorers and historians have been fascinated by the mysterious disappearance of an ancient civilization that once thrived in the dense rainforests of South America. The city, believed to have been a center of trade and culture, vanished without a trace, leaving behind only ruins and unanswered questions. Archaeologists have uncovered remnants of towering stone structures, intricate carvings, and vast underground reservoirs, suggesting that the inhabitants were highly advanced. Despite these discoveries, the reasons behind the civilization’s sudden collapse remain unknown. Some scholars propose that environmental STUDENTS, 2017/2025. changes led to food shortages, while others believe that warfare or disease played a crucial role. Regardless of the cause, the city’s disappearance continues to intrigue researchers worldwide. 2. Recent excavations have provided new insights into the lives of the people who once called this city home. Pottery fragments, jewelry, and primitive tools indicate that the civilization had a complex society with skilled artisans, traders, and builders. In addition, the discovery of an elaborate writing system suggests that they had a rich literary tradition. However, without a complete understanding of their language, researchers struggle to piece together the full story of this lost world. Even the city’s name remains uncertain, as different sources refer to it by various titles. These challenges make it difficult to reconstruct the past with absolute certainty. 3. One prevailing theory suggests that deforestation and soil erosion may have led to agricultural decline, forcing the population to migrate elsewhere. Evidence of abandoned farmlands and deteriorating irrigation systems supports this claim. If the city’s people could no longer grow enough food to sustain themselves, their survival would have been threatened. This environmental catastrophe could have sparked internal conflict, causing the once-thriving civilization to fall apart. Over time, the jungle reclaimed the land, burying the city beneath layers of vegetation. 4. Another hypothesis is that a powerful enemy invaded and destroyed the city. Archaeological evidence of burned structures and scattered weapons suggests that a battle may have taken place. Ancient texts from neighboring societies describe a ruthless conqueror who sought to expand his empire at any cost. If true, this theory would mean that the city was not abandoned voluntarily but was instead the victim of a brutal campaign. Still, some researchers remain skeptical, as no mass graves or large-scale destruction have been discovered. 5. Disease is yet another possible explanation for the city’s demise. Some experts argue that a deadly epidemic, possibly introduced by foreign traders, could have wiped out much of the population. If the disease spread rapidly, survivors may have been forced to flee, leaving their once-prosperous city behind. This theory is supported by skeletal remains that show signs of malnutrition and illness, though conclusive evidence is still lacking. 6. Despite centuries of research, the fate of this lost civilization remains uncertain. Modern technology, including satellite imaging and DNA analysis, continues to provide valuable clues. STUDENTS, 2017/2025. However, with each new discovery, more questions arise, deepening the mystery. The search for answers is ongoing, and the truth may never be fully known. 7. Ultimately, the story of the vanished city serves as a cautionary tale. Whether destroyed by nature, war, or disease, its downfall reminds us of the fragility of even the greatest civilizations. Understanding what happened to this ancient society could offer important lessons for the future, helping modern civilizations avoid a similar fate. Source: https://c/67adc8e1-9644-800c-826d-c1dcbd954525"
